    "QuestionText": "\u221a3 is irrational. Proof is by:",
    "Options": [
      "A) Induction",
      "B) Direct proof",
      "C) Contradiction",
      "D) Construction"
    ],
    "CorrectAnswer": "C",
    "Topic": "Mathematics - Number Systems",
    "SubTopic": "Irrational Numbers",
    "Difficulty": "Olympiad",
    "Explanation": "Proof by contradiction: Assume \u221a3 = p/q (lowest terms). Then 3 = p\u00b2/q\u00b2, so p\u00b2 = 3q\u00b2, meaning 3|p\u00b2, so 3|p. Let p=3k. Then 9k\u00b2=3q\u00b2, q\u00b2=3k\u00b2, so 3|q. But this contradicts p,q having no common factor."
  },
